            | matrix performs much worse over the LUTCHI (D65/WF), and Breneman (3), (4), (8), and (9) datasets.Perhaps this is the natural result of adding the nesting constraint to the optimum solution search. Theoptimum is no longer unconstrained, and so the cost function must degrade. On the other hand, it can benoted that the original
